      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was kinda hoping I would get used to this over time but it's been a couple weeks and this still really throws me off. My original post focuses more on the design aspect of this change so I thought I'd comment on this from a muscle-memory perspective.\n\nThis change never fails to make me glance around in confusion for a second when looking for anything after the \"Updated\" panel. In my proposed change, everything would remain identical to the way it was before, with only the \"Size\" panel being in a different place. I think making users re-learn where a single UI element is would be way more elegant than cluttering half of them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
